WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.728
[piano instrumental]

00:00:04.728 --> 00:00:19.273
[televison jingle]

00:00:19.273 --> 00:00:20.400
[static]

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.680
America is the greatest country on Earth!

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:24.640
The strongest,

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:25.920
the richest,

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:28.240
the most powerful country on Earth.

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:29.840
As an American, I'm sure you've heard that

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:32.240
roughly 135 times a year.

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:34.880
235 if you go to public school

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:37.760
335 if you go to a christian academy

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:39.920
We're told that Americans have the best lives

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:41.440
of any people in the world.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:42.880
That we have low taxes,

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:43.680
small government,

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:45.600
and the highest living standards on Earth.

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:48.960
And, most inaccurately, that we're the freest.

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:51.975
Well it is partly true,

00:00:51.975 --> 00:00:53.534
America is the richest country,

00:00:53.534 --> 00:00:56.080
not just in the world, but in the history of the world.

00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:59.920
It's really hard to&nbsp;comprehend&nbsp;just how rich we are.

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:03.040
We have 18 million people who are millionaires.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:07.440
American households own about 100 trillion dollars

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:10.160
in wealth, an almost unthinkable amount of money

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:14.240
Okay, so America is the richest country ever

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:16.960
but there's a curious paradox.

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:19.440
most Americans actually have a much worse

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:20.960
standard of living than people who live

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:22.480
in poorer countries like

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:24.000
Germany, or Finland, or Britain.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:25.760
But how can that be?

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:27.040
That shouldn't make any sense.

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:29.600
Well, here's the shitty deal.

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:32.400
Americans get significantly worse services

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:35.600
because our tax dollars don't fund them.

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:37.680
So of course our services are worse

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:39.520
and thus, we enjoy less happy lives than

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:41.360
people who live in the aforementioned countries.

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:44.880
Not that difficult a concept to conceive, really.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:47.280
"You get what you pay for!" said the cartoon dog

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:48.560
to the other cartoon dog.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.360
And while you might think the reason American

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:53.520
tax dollars don't fund as many services

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:56.400
is because we pay lower taxes than other countries

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:58.160
that's not even true!

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:01.680
When you add federal,&nbsp;
state,&nbsp;local, and sales taxes and

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:04.560
include other costs and&nbsp;services&nbsp;that our taxes don't cover

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:06.240
but other countries taxes do,

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:09.680
like our uniquely high health insurance premiums,

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:11.680
you'll find that Americans actually give away

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:14.960
MORE of their wages than&nbsp;most&nbsp;of the developed world.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:17.120
For example,

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:19.760
in Canada, for a married worker with two kids,

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:21.840
all the previously mentioned costs combined,

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:23.920
from taxes to health insurance premiums,

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:26.880
make up only 11 of the average wage

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:28.720
in the uk it's just about 26%.

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:31.760
Meanwhile, once you tack on the cost of

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:34.080
our outlandish health insurance premiums,

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:38.320
you're spending a whopping 43% of your paycheck

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:41.040
that's more than France Finland Sweden and Norway.

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:44.480
In real reality, Americans keep much less of

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:46.560
what we own than in other countries.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:47.440
In other countries,

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:49.600
their government takes a bit more tax

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:51.600
but then gives that money back to their citizens

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:53.120
in the form of health care,

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:54.640
or job support,

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:56.240
or a general safety net for

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:57.680
all vulnerable citizens,

00:02:57.680 --> 00:02:59.600
no matter how dusky they are.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:04.160
So what do Americans get for the money we pay in?

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:05.360
Well sure, we get

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:06.640
a crumbling infrastructure,

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:07.680
shameful homelessness,

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:10.080
and millions of hungry, neglected children

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:13.920
BUT we also get some of the worst services in

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:14.880
the developed world.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:17.120
Again, our healthcare.

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:20.800
American healthcare&nbsp;
is&nbsp;simultaneously the most expensive,

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:21.920
the least efficient,

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:24.080
and the least effective healthcare system in

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:25.120
the developed world.

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:28.000
He-hey! The devil's trifecta.

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:31.200
and in exchange for this extremely expensive,

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:33.600
inefficient healthcare system, what do we get?

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:35.760
Well we get some of the worst health outcomes

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:36.960
in the developed world.

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:38.960
We have fewer hospital beds per capita

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:41.120
than people in Turkey or Brunei

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:43.360
americans have a lower life expectancy than

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:45.600
people in Lebanon or Cuba

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:49.040
and in the Mississippi&nbsp;Delta,&nbsp;
and much of Appalachia?

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:52.400
Life expectancy is lower than in Bangladesh.

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:57.360
In fact, in 2017, the United Nations sent

00:03:57.360 --> 00:03:59.600
a commissioner to West Virginia to document

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:01.120
what he saw and he described

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:04.960
"third world conditions&nbsp;of absolute poverty."

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:08.960
We even have a higher infant mortality rate

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:11.840
than people in Russia and Serbia.

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:16.160
In every single metric, America does worse

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:17.280
across the board.

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:21.200
So why is healthcare so expensive?

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:23.120
Because it's so complicated.

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:25.040
You have to look for in-network physicians,

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:26.960
schedule an established care appointment,

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:28.720
beg for coverage from your insurance company

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:30.240
that couldn't care less about you,

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:32.480
and that's if you're lucky&nbsp;enough&nbsp;
to have good insurance!

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:35.440
Compare that to Britain, and all of those other

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:37.600
evil socialist-like countries

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:38.240
where it's simple:

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:42.160
public hospitals provide&nbsp;
free&nbsp;treatment to people who need it.

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:43.620
That's it

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:45.600
I'll repeat that.

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:49.760
Public hospitals provide&nbsp;
free&nbsp;treatment to people who need it.

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:52.000
And here's the best part:

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:54.000
even though britain offers health care for free

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:56.160
their system is actually a lot cheaper to run

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:56.720
than ours.

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:00.000
Per capita healthcare&nbsp;spending in the U.S. is almost

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.600
three times what it is in Britain,

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:04.160
and almost five times what Canadians spend.

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:07.200
In fact Americans spend the most per person

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:10.400
of any country in the world for health care.

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:13.120
"But the free market is more efficient" you screech.

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:17.440
But in America, private systems&nbsp;often aren't efficient at all

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:19.280
private drug companies have an incentive to

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:22.240
charge whatever they can get&nbsp;away with for pharmaceuticals.

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:27.280
In Canada, a carton of insulin costs about 20 bucks.

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:30.960
In the U.S. it costs 300 bucks.

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:32.960
And with private insurance&nbsp;companies footing the bill,

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:35.280
hospitals have an incentive to get as much money

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:36.880
out of patients as possible too.

00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:41.280
In 2015 the average cost of an mri scan

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:44.880
in the U.S. was $1119.

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:49.040
But it was only $215 in Australia.

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:51.840
Spain? About 181 bucks.

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:54.000
And our health care system is so inefficient

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:57.437
that we spend over a third of&nbsp;our costs on-

00:05:57.437 --> 00:05:58.671
administration.

00:05:59.034 --> 00:06:01.200
The United States spends significantly more

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:04.400
on administration than we spend on preventative

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:06.160
or long-term health care.

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:08.560
That's just not smart

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:12.640
"Okay, we get it. We all know&nbsp;that American health care

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:14.880
is so much more expensive," you say.

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:17.840
"But that's the cost of having the freest freedom

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:19.680
in God's favorite country!"

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:20.939
Well... guess what?

00:06:20.939 --> 00:06:24.160
Medical procedures&nbsp;that are totally free in Britain,

00:06:24.346 --> 00:06:25.402
like giving birth,

00:06:25.402 --> 00:06:29.120
cost tens of thousands&nbsp;of dollars in the United States.

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:31.360
I mean you want to talk about the cost of freedom.

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:33.200
Sadly, because of these high costs,

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:35.440
Americans often avoid going to the doctor,

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:38.160
something almost half the population say they do.

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:41.338
with shoddy or&nbsp;non-existent health insurance,

00:06:41.338 --> 00:06:43.760
Americans will wait until their&nbsp;conditions force them into

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:45.680
the emergency room, where treatment is

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:46.800
far more expensive.

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:50.400
Again, not a smart system.

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:53.840
Quite often, they end up putting&nbsp;off medical visits and dying.

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:58.160
Susan Finley, a 53 year old&nbsp;Walmart employee in Colorado,

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:00.720
got pneumonia and took one day off of work

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:02.640
beyond what Walmart's policy allows.

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:05.440
So of course, Walmart's going to Walmart

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:07.760
which they did, by firing her.

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:10.080
Without her job she lost her nominal health care coverage,

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:12.080
she struggled to find new work,

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:14.080
and after avoiding a visit to the doctor for

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:17.680
flu-like symptoms, she was&nbsp;found dead in her apartment.

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:24.000
When Americans do manage to get treated,

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:26.000
they frequently can't afford it.

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:28.000
Simple, life-saving treatments can cost

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:30.160
tens or hundreds of thousands of dollars and

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:31.600
if they don't have really good insurance

00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:33.810
they're forced to take on medical debt.

00:07:33.810 --> 00:07:36.160
Tens of millions of Americans owe medical debt,

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:38.480
often into the tens of thousands of dollars.

00:07:38.480 --> 00:07:41.840
Meanwhile in a country like Britain or Norway,

00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:44.000
Medical debt is almost unheard of.

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:47.440
But hey, that's why GoFundMe is such a critical

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:49.040
component of American health care.

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:53.280
One in three GoFundMe campaigns&nbsp;is now for medical bills.

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:54.240
I'll repeat that,

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:58.960
one in three GoFundMe campaigns&nbsp;
is now for medical bills.

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:02.720
America is such a strong,&nbsp;powerful, rich, and great country

00:08:02.720 --> 00:08:05.760
that its citizens have to&nbsp;beg strangers on the internet

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:08.240
for money so they can get life-saving treatments

00:08:08.240 --> 00:08:11.840
that are FREE in the rest of the developed world.

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:15.200
But hey, that's just healthcare.

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:17.520
Americans get terrible deals wherever you look.

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:19.520
Let's take work, for example.

00:08:20.320 --> 00:08:22.320
Americans work longer hours than people in

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:23.760
any other rich country in the world,

00:08:23.760 --> 00:08:26.240
and that's not because they&nbsp;enjoy sleep deprivation

00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:28.560
and not seeing their families for days at a time.

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:33.120
It's because they don't want&nbsp;to starve, or freeze, or die.

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:36.640
See, America has the least&nbsp;generous job support programs,

00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:38.320
the least generous family benefits,

00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:40.480
and the least generous unemployment benefits

00:08:40.480 --> 00:08:41.920
of any wealthy country.

00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:44.320
It's one of the only countries on Earth

00:08:44.320 --> 00:08:47.280
that doesn't guarantee paid time off for vacations.

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:49.600
It doesn't even help provide&nbsp;paid time off for parents

00:08:49.600 --> 00:08:51.280
who JUST had a child.

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:53.680
And it's not coincidental that we're also

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:56.480
one of the most hostile&nbsp;countries to workers rights.

00:08:56.480 --> 00:08:59.040
America has one of the lowest unionization rates

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:00.240
in the entire world.

00:09:00.880 --> 00:09:04.080
Maybe this deprivation, our refusal to give people

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:06.640
the means to lead a good, dignified life, commensurate

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:08.496
with how rich our country is,

00:09:08.496 --> 00:09:11.200
can explain a bit of what we've seen in the United States

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:12.320
over the last few decades.

00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:13.920
Fraying communities,

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:16.160
rising rates of depression and suicide,

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:18.320
huge numbers of deaths from drug overdoses.

00:09:18.960 --> 00:09:20.880
These so-called "deaths of despair,"

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:21.771
suicide,

00:09:21.771 --> 00:09:22.498
drug overdoses,

00:09:22.498 --> 00:09:24.160
alcoholic liver disease,

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:27.040
they're one big reason why&nbsp;American life expectancy

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:30.320
has actually started to&nbsp;
decline over the last few years.

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:34.080
And with such poor conditions, it's not a surprise

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:37.120
that poverty is so rampant in the United States.

00:09:37.120 --> 00:09:39.040
America devotes a smaller percentage of

00:09:39.040 --> 00:09:41.440
spending on social welfare than any other

00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:43.600
industrialized economy because,

00:09:44.720 --> 00:09:45.845
say it with me,

00:09:45.845 --> 00:09:47.120
socialism is evil.

00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:48.586
It's evil!

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:51.360
Go to Denmark and try telling those

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:53.760
happy, healthy families&nbsp;enjoying their paid vacation

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:56.640
that their system of government is evil.

00:09:57.520 --> 00:09:58.336
Guess what?

00:09:58.336 --> 00:10:01.600
I guarantee they'll&nbsp;know you're an American

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:03.600
But I digress,

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:06.720
America also has the highest rate of child poverty

00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:09.120
of any developed country,&nbsp;and the highest percentage

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:11.280
of workers earning significantly less than

00:10:11.280 --> 00:10:13.200
the national median income.

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:15.280
THAT seems pretty evil to me.

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:17.840
Especially since such a tiny fraction

00:10:17.840 --> 00:10:19.840
take as much of your money from themselves

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:22.000
and their families as you will let them.

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:24.400
All the while both parties smile

00:10:24.400 --> 00:10:26.284
and shake hands.

00:10:26.284 --> 00:10:28.612
Across every single metric,

00:10:28.612 --> 00:10:32.187
no people accept a worse deal than Americans today.

00:10:32.187 --> 00:10:33.161
high taxes,

00:10:33.161 --> 00:10:34.517
high costs of living,

00:10:34.517 --> 00:10:36.897
for next to nothing in return from the government.

00:10:37.206 --> 00:10:38.586
The most expensive health care system,

00:10:38.586 --> 00:10:40.640
for the worst health outcomes.

00:10:41.280 --> 00:10:42.960
More money taken from workers,

00:10:42.960 --> 00:10:45.280
for the highest rate of child poverty.

00:10:45.280 --> 00:10:47.760
We are the richest country&nbsp;in the history of the world,

00:10:47.760 --> 00:10:51.440
but we have fewer miles of&nbsp;high-speed rail than Uzbekistan.

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:54.000
We are the greatest country in the world,

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:56.640
yet we have the most people&nbsp;in prison of any country

00:10:56.640 --> 00:10:59.520
and the highest incarceration rate as well.

00:10:59.520 --> 00:11:04.480
And a higher rate of police&nbsp;killings than in Angola, and Sudan.

00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:06.000
America is bad at everything because

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:08.000
instead of choosing to make life better

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:08.593
for people,

00:11:08.593 --> 00:11:11.158
through a public health care system or

00:11:11.158 --> 00:11:12.636
more generous child care policies,

00:11:12.636 --> 00:11:13.712
or better public transit,

00:11:13.712 --> 00:11:15.072
or programs that allow people to

00:11:15.072 --> 00:11:16.560
spend more time with their families,

00:11:17.200 --> 00:11:19.440
American law is designed and crafted

00:11:19.440 --> 00:11:22.880
to protect a class of&nbsp;parasitical middleman industries.

00:11:22.880 --> 00:11:25.280
Instead of using a proportionally tiny piece

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:27.920
of the massive amount of&nbsp;the wealth in this country

00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:30.800
to make people's lives healthier and happier.

00:11:31.520 --> 00:11:33.200
Most of our elected leaders are,

00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:34.560
and have been for generations,

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:36.640
engaged in a massive project of

00:11:36.640 --> 00:11:37.517
looting.

00:11:37.517 --> 00:11:41.440
Gently and lovingly guiding as much money as possible

00:11:41.440 --> 00:11:42.640
from working people into the

00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:45.200
pockets of the well-connected and the ultra-rich.

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:48.480
Think about that as we start hearing about

00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:49.840
the inevitable rise in

00:11:49.840 --> 00:11:50.960
homelessness,

00:11:50.960 --> 00:11:51.840
poverty,

00:11:51.840 --> 00:11:52.800
starvation,

00:11:52.800 --> 00:11:54.560
and sickness that will occur during

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:56.080
these coming months and years

00:11:56.720 --> 00:11:57.440
in the greatest,

00:11:58.000 --> 00:11:59.120
strongest,

00:11:59.120 --> 00:11:59.760
richest,

00:11:59.760 --> 00:12:01.120
most powerful country

